Decko TypeScript port
====================

This is a modified TypeScript derivative of Decko, targeting card 1.110.0 and
decko 0.20.0. HANDOVER-MANIFEST.json records the packaging source in sourceCommit
and the designated engine source in engineCommit. This notice is not a build,
comparison or release result; those require separate receipts. It is not an upstream
release. Decko upstream: https://github.com/decko-commons/decko and https://decko.org.
Upstream authors include Ethan McCutchen, Philipp Kühl, Gerry Gleason and the
Decko contributors. Ported code retains upstream copyright and
GPL-3.0-or-later terms; the complete GPL version 3 is in LICENSE.

RUBY-MAP.md records the Ruby citations found in every packaged TypeScript
module. Per-file source comments remain the detailed provenance record.

Third-party components keep their own terms and notices. vendor/ and
fixtures/vendor/ include license and provenance files beside the components;
the edge asset snapshots embed those notices. This includes Bootstrap,
Bootswatch, Select2, jQuery components, Apache-2.0 Bootstrap Colorpicker,
LGPL-2.1 TinyMCE, the MIT/BSD Uglifier inputs, MIT LibSass, OFL fonts and
Font Awesome. tools/libsass/libsass/ includes the compiler source and its
MIT license; utf8-cpp there carries BSL-1.0 in its header. The source headers
also attribute ports from ActiveSupport, kramdown, CodeRay, Haml and Rails.
HTML extraction dependencies have notices under vendor/html-text-licenses/.
The complete CodeRay 1.1.3 notice is in vendor/coderay-1.1.3/LICENSE.
Complete upstream grants also accompany the kramdown, ActiveSupport and Haml
ports in their named vendor directories, with their retrieval sources recorded.
Dependency versions and integrity records are in package-lock.json.

Redistribution review must check corresponding-source and modification
requirements for every included component, including LGPL TinyMCE and compiled
assets inside synthetic decks. A top-level GPL declaration alone is not a
completed review of those obligations. No commercial license is asserted.
The package is held for that review and approval before any sharing.

TinyMCE 5.10.7 is included as minified library bytes and inside fixture bundles.
Its complete official preferred-form source tree accompanies those bytes under
third-party-source/tinymce-5.10.7/upstream/, with the full upstream license,
build scripts, workspace manifests and lockfile. PROVENANCE.md and
SOURCE-MANIFEST.json beside it pin the official tag commit and every raw source
file. No deferred distributor offer or prior recipient delivery is asserted.
Independent review of this exact source-supply material remains required.

Finite held-source identity reviews do not approve a later generated package.
Final source-supply, privacy, sharing approval and native POSIX export-mode
acceptance remain open. This notice supplies no current compatibility result,
source-to-binary rebuild claim or published binary checksum assertion.
